indexes work.

00:44:51.731 --> 00:44:54.180
So, to overcome the
problem that we have,

00:44:54.181 --> 00:44:57.355
a very efficient way to
overfit to something,

00:44:57.356 --> 00:44:59.550
we came up with this structure

00:44:59.551 --> 00:45:01.570
which we call the
recursive model index,

00:45:01.571 --> 00:45:03.890
but you can best think
of it's just like

00:45:03.891 --> 00:45:07.815
an expert model where one model,

00:45:07.816 --> 00:45:09.330
the top one, picks

00:45:09.331 --> 00:45:10.380
another model which was

00:45:10.381 --> 00:45:12.580
an expert for
certain range of the data.

00:45:12.581 --> 00:45:14.570
Right. So, we have one
model at the top which

00:45:14.571 --> 00:45:16.330
takes the key,
makes a prediction,

00:45:16.331 --> 00:45:17.395
based on the prediction,

00:45:17.396 --> 00:45:19.945
you pick another model
which no set area better,

00:45:19.946 --> 00:45:21.910
which might pick another
model. All right.

00:45:21.911 --> 00:45:23.845
So, the nice thing about that is,

00:45:23.846 --> 00:45:26.800
it can be very
efficiently implemented.

00:45:26.801 --> 00:45:29.555
Let's assume I have
a top model f 0.

00:45:29.556 --> 00:45:31.810
F, models on stage two,

00:45:31.811 --> 00:45:33.940
that's just an array of models.

00:45:33.941 --> 00:45:35.470
So, what I'm actually doing,

00:45:35.471 --> 00:45:37.450
is just like I execute
the first model which gives me

00:45:37.451 --> 00:45:38.630
an index position into

00:45:38.631 --> 00:45:40.420
the array of models
of the second stage,

00:45:40.421 --> 00:45:42.080
which then can execute
which gives me

00:45:42.081 --> 00:45:44.520
the final position if I
have a two stage model.

00:45:44.521 --> 00:45:47.370
If I now, for everything
don't use neural nets,

00:45:47.371 --> 00:45:49.480
but let's assume just
like linear regression,

00:45:49.481 --> 00:45:51.230
the whole lookup, as you can see

00:45:51.231 --> 00:45:53.305
down here takes me
two multiplies,

00:45:53.306 --> 00:45:55.530
two additions, and
one area look up.

00:45:55.531 --> 00:45:58.735
This is the execution of
the index, that's it.

00:45:58.736 --> 00:46:02.145
There's some code necessary
for boundary checks,

00:46:02.146 --> 00:46:04.410
but it turns out you
can also avoid that.

00:46:04.411 --> 00:46:07.110
You just need to change
the learning a little

00:46:07.111 --> 00:46:08.560
bit so that the boundaries

00:46:08.561 --> 00:46:10.750
to do checks whenever necessary.

00:46:11.460 --> 00:46:14.730
Furthermore, you can,
in some cases even

00:46:14.731 --> 00:46:17.830
replace some of the modes
using normal B-trees.

00:46:17.831 --> 00:46:19.220
Right. So, if you say, "Okay,

00:46:19.221 --> 00:46:21.790
in a certain area
the normal linear model,

00:46:21.791 --> 00:46:23.400
or neural net, or
