So, it doesn't work.

00:47:21.071 --> 00:47:22.520
What we did here, is just like we

00:47:22.521 --> 00:47:24.680
compared to a cash optimized,

00:47:24.681 --> 00:47:26.525
and read optimized Be-tree

00:47:26.526 --> 00:47:29.435
tuned out to get
the best lookup performance,

00:47:29.436 --> 00:47:31.460
and compared to
our learned indexes,

00:47:31.461 --> 00:47:33.740
and what you see
is just overall we

00:47:33.741 --> 00:47:36.780
get up to a factor of two

00:47:36.781 --> 00:47:39.970
faster and save up

00:47:39.971 --> 00:47:43.090
to one order or even
more in main memory.

00:47:43.091 --> 00:47:44.845
We also compared us against

00:47:44.846 --> 00:47:46.940
other states of
that index structures,

00:47:46.941 --> 00:47:49.215
for example files,
