00:48:03.211 --> 00:48:05.410
is like a dominant solution.

00:48:05.980 --> 00:48:08.780
So what about like
our assumption I did in

00:48:08.781 --> 00:48:11.465
the beginning about
'Inserts' and 'Paging'.

00:48:11.466 --> 00:48:13.640
First of all, 'Inserts' might not

00:48:13.641 --> 00:48:15.865
be such a big problem in that.

00:48:15.866 --> 00:48:18.800
So let's assume that
your 'Inserts' follow

00:48:18.801 --> 00:48:22.485
roughly the data distribution
what you have learned.

00:48:22.486 --> 00:48:24.370
In that sense, you don't need to

00:48:24.371 --> 00:48:26.390
rebalance the model, right.

00:48:26.391 --> 00:48:27.570
You don't need to change it.

00:48:27.571 --> 00:48:29.380
You can just reuse
the model and make

00:48:29.381 --> 00:48:32.050
space wherever you want
to insert something.

00:48:32.051 --> 00:48:34.100
This is particularly
easy to see if

00:48:34.101 --> 00:48:36.020
you have mostly like 'Inserts'.

00:48:36.021 --> 00:48:38.755
Let's assume you have
timestamps for IoT devices.

00:48:38.756 --> 00:48:40.410
The timestamps normally increase.

00:48:40.411 --> 00:48:41.800
It might increase with
the same patterns

00:48:41.801 --> 00:48:43.285
what you have
observed in the past,

00:48:43.286 --> 00:48:45.075
so the model simply generalizes.

00:48:45.076 --> 00:48:48.035
As a B-tree, you have to
